<p dir=3D"auto">The Extensible Hypertext Markup Language, or XHTML, has two=
 important notes for front end developers.</p>
<ol dir=3D"auto">
<li>It needs to be well formed, meaning all elements need to be closed and =
nested correctly or you will return errors.</li>
<li>Since it is more strict than HTML is requires less pre-processing by th=
e browser, which may improve your sites performance.</li>
</ol>
