<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>1. Async:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Downloads the script file during HTML parsing and will paus=
e the HTML parser to execute it when it has finished downloading.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Example:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"highlight highlight-text-html-basic notranslate position-rela=
tive overflow-auto" dir=3D"auto"><pre><span class=3D"pl-c">&lt;!-- </span>
<span class=3D"pl-c">    With async (asynchronous), browser will continue t=
o load the HTML </span>
<span class=3D"pl-c">    page and render it while the browser load and exec=
ute the script at the same time. </span>
<span class=3D"pl-c">--&gt;</span>
<span class=3D"pl-c">&lt;!-- Google Analytics is usually added like this --=
&gt;</span>
<span class=3D"pl-kos">&lt;</span><span class=3D"pl-ent">script</span> <spa=
n class=3D"pl-c1">async</span> <span class=3D"pl-c1">src</span>=3D"<span cl=
ass=3D"pl-s">https://google-analytics.com/analytics.js</span>"<span class=
=3D"pl-kos">&gt;</span><span class=3D"pl-kos">&lt;/</span><span class=3D"pl=
-ent">script</span><span class=3D"pl-kos">&gt;</span></pre><div class=3D"ze=
roclipboard-container">
