<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>2. Defer:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Defer downloads the script file during HTML parsing and wil=
l only execute it after the HTML parser has completed. Not all browsers sup=
port this.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Example:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"highlight highlight-text-html-basic notranslate position-rela=
tive overflow-auto" dir=3D"auto"><pre><span class=3D"pl-c">&lt;!-- </span>
<span class=3D"pl-c">    With defer, browser will run your script when the =
page finished parsing. </span>
<span class=3D"pl-c">    (not necessary finishing downloading all image fil=
es. This is good.) </span>
<span class=3D"pl-c">--&gt;</span>
<span class=3D"pl-kos">&lt;</span><span class=3D"pl-ent">script</span> <spa=
n class=3D"pl-c1">defer</span> <span class=3D"pl-c1">src</span>=3D"<span cl=
ass=3D"pl-s">myscript.js</span>"<span class=3D"pl-kos">&gt;</span><span cla=
ss=3D"pl-kos">&lt;/</span><span class=3D"pl-ent">script</span><span class=
=3D"pl-kos">&gt;</span></pre><div class=3D"zeroclipboard-container">
