<p dir=3D"auto">Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS) is a W3C spec that all=
ows cross-domain communication from the browser. By building on top of the =
XMLHttpRequest object, CORS allows developers to work with the same idioms =
as same-domain requests. CORS gives web servers cross-domain access control=
s, which enable secure cross-domain data transfers.</p>
