<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>
<p dir=3D"auto">Graceful degradation is when you initially serve the best p=
ossible user experience, with all modern functionality, but use feature det=
ection to =E2=80=9Cgracefully degrade=E2=80=9D parts of your application wi=
th a fallback or polyfill.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p dir=3D"auto">Progressive enhancement ensures a page works at the lowest =
expected abilities of browsers. So if you have a JavaScript web application=
 that enhances a persons ability to send information to a database with fea=
tures like ajax =E2=80=93 at the very least you need to provide the ability=
 for a person to send that same information without JavaScript enabled. In =
this case a simple form with full-page refresh will do what you need.</p>
</li>
</ul>
