<p dir=3D"auto">In <strong>Quirks mode</strong>, layout emulates nonstandar=
d behavior in Navigator 4 and Internet Explorer 5. This is essential in ord=
er to support websites that were built before the widespread adoption of we=
b standards. In <strong>Standards mode</strong>, the behavior is described =
by the HTML and CSS specifications.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">For HTML documents, browsers use a <code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&=
gt;</code> in the beginning of the document to decide whether to handle it =
in quirks mode or standards mode.</p>
