<p dir=3D"auto">The primary difference between div and span tag is their de=
fault behavior. By default, a <code>&lt;div&gt;</code> is a <strong>block-l=
evel-element</strong> and a <code>&lt;span&gt;</code> is an <strong>inline =
element</strong>.</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li><code>&lt;div&gt;</code> is a block level element which means it will r=
ender it on it's own line with a width of a 100% of the parent element.</li=
>
<li><code>&lt;span&gt;</code> is an inline element which means it will rend=
er on the same line as the previous element, if it is also an inline elemen=
t, and it's width will be determined by it's content.</li>
</ul>
