<p dir=3D"auto">In HTML, <strong>optional closing tags</strong> are tags wh=
ere the browser automatically closes them when it encounters a new tag, so =
the end tag is not required.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Common examples: <code>&lt;p&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;li&gt;</=
code>, <code>&lt;td&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;tr&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;th&gt;</=
code>, <code>&lt;html&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;body&gt;</code></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">The full list of optional tags includes:</p>
