<p dir=3D"auto">HTML events are actions or occurrences that happen in the b=
rowser =E2=80=94 triggered by the user or by the browser itself. JavaScript=
 can listen for these events and execute code in response.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Events can originate from:</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li><strong>User interaction</strong> =E2=80=94 mouse clicks, key presses, =
form input</li>
<li><strong>Browser lifecycle</strong> =E2=80=94 page load, resize, scroll<=
/li>
<li><strong>Media</strong> =E2=80=94 video play/pause/end</li>
<li><strong>Network</strong> =E2=80=94 online/offline state changes</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>How to handle events:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>1. Inline HTML attribute (not recommended):</strong=
></p>
