<p dir=3D"auto">When an event occurs on a nested element, it propagates thr=
ough the DOM in two phases:</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>1. Capturing phase (top =E2=86=92 target)</strong>
The event travels from the <code>document</code> root down to the target el=
ement.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>2. Bubbling phase (target =E2=86=92 top)</strong>
After reaching the target, the event bubbles back up through its ancestors.=
</p>
