<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Event delegation</strong> is a technique where a si=
ngle event listener is attached to a <strong>parent element</strong> instea=
d of adding listeners to each child element individually. It leverages even=
t bubbling to handle events from child elements.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Why use it:</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Fewer event listeners =E2=86=92 better memory performance</li>
<li>Works for dynamically added elements</li>
<li>Cleaner code</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Example without delegation (inefficient):</strong><=
/p>
<div class=3D"highlight highlight-text-html-basic notranslate position-rela=
tive overflow-auto" dir=3D"auto"><pre><span class=3D"pl-kos">&lt;</span><sp=
