<p dir=3D"auto">HTML5 provides <strong>client-side form validation</strong>=
 without JavaScript, using built-in validation attributes. The browser chec=
ks these constraints before submitting.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Built-in validation attributes:</strong></p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Attribute</th>
<th>Applies to</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>required</code></td>
<td>Most inputs</td>
<td>Field must not be empty</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>minlength</code> / <code>maxlength</code></td>
<td><code>text</code>, <code>email</code>, <code>password</code>, etc.</td>
<td>Min/max character count</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>min</code> / <code>max</code></td>
<td><code>number</code>, <code>date</code>, <code>range</code></td>
<td>Min/max value</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>step</code></td>
<td><code>number</code>, <code>range</code>, <code>date</code></td>
<td>Valid value increments</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>pattern</code></td>
<td><code>text</code>, <code>email</code>, <code>url</code>, <code>tel</cod=
e></td>
<td>Must match a regex</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>type</code></td>
<td><code>&lt;input&gt;</code></td>
<td>Validates format (e.g., <code>email</code>, <code>url</code>, <code>num=
ber</code>)</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
