<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>2. Meter Tag</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Indicates a numeric value that falls within a range. The ta=
g supports a number of attributes:
value: If you don't specify a value, the first numeric value inside the <co=
de>&lt;meter&gt;&lt;/meter&gt;</code> pair becomes the value.</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li><strong>max</strong>: The maximum possible value of the item.</li>
<li><strong>min</strong>: The minimum possible value of the item.</li>
<li><strong>high</strong>: If the value can be defined as a range, this is =
the high end of the range.</li>
<li><strong>low</strong>: If the value can defined as a range, this is the =
low end of that range.</li>
<li><strong>optimum</strong>: The optimal value of the element.</li>
</ul>
