<p dir=3D"auto">Both <code>&lt;th&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;td&gt;</code> de=
fine cells in a table row, but they have distinct purposes:</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th></th>
<th><code>&lt;th&gt;</code> (Table Header)</th>
<th><code>&lt;td&gt;</code> (Table Data)</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Purpose</strong></td>
<td>Header cell =E2=80=94 labels a column or row</td>
<td>Data cell =E2=80=94 contains actual data</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Default style</strong></td>
<td>Bold, centered</td>
<td>Normal weight, left-aligned</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Accessibility</strong></td>
<td>Semantically marks up heading content</td>
<td>Contains content only</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong><code>scope</code> attribute</strong></td>
<td>Supports <code>scope</code> to define what it headers</td>
<td>Does not use <code>scope</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Usage</strong></td>
<td>Inside <code>&lt;thead&gt;</code> rows, or as row headers in <code>&lt;=
tbody&gt;</code></td>
<td>Inside <code>&lt;tbody&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;tfoot&gt;</code> rows</=
td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
