<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>When to use <code>&lt;dl&gt;</code> vs <code>&lt;ul=
&gt;</code>:</strong></p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Use <code>&lt;dl&gt;</code></th>
<th>Use <code>&lt;ul&gt;</code></th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Key-value pairs (term: definition)</td>
<td>Simple list of items</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Glossaries, FAQs</td>
<td>Navigation menus</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Metadata (author, date, category)</td>
<td>Feature lists</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Contact information</td>
<td>Tag lists</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
<blockquote>
<p dir=3D"auto"><code>&lt;dl&gt;</code> is often misused for layout indenta=
tion. Use it only when the content is genuinely a set of term=E2=80=93descr=
iption pairs.</p>
</blockquote>
