<p dir=3D"auto">Iframes have significant performance implications because e=
ach one is a <strong>fully independent browsing context</strong> with its o=
wn DOM, CSSOM, JavaScript engine instance, and resource pipeline.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Performance costs:</strong></p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Cost</th>
<th>Detail</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Memory</strong></td>
<td>Each iframe has its own JS heap, DOM tree, and style system</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Network</strong></td>
<td>A fresh HTTP pipeline per iframe; no connection sharing with parent</td=
>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>CPU</strong></td>
<td>Separate render pipeline and JS execution context</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Load blocking</strong></td>
<td>Synchronous iframes (no <code>loading=3D"lazy"</code>) block <code>wind=
ow.onload</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Third-party scripts</strong></td>
<td>Ads/analytics in iframes may load dozens of sub-resources</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
