<p dir=3D"auto">Both specify a URL, but they serve different purposes and t=
rigger different browser behavior:</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th></th>
<th><code>href</code></th>
<th><code>src</code></th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Stands for</strong></td>
<td>Hypertext Reference</td>
<td>Source</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Used on</strong></td>
<td><code>&lt;a&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;link&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;base&gt;</=
code>, <code>&lt;area&gt;</code></td>
<td><code>&lt;img&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;script&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;iframe=
&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;audio&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;video&gt;</code>, <code>=
&lt;input&gt;</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Purpose</strong></td>
<td>Points to a <strong>linked</strong> resource</td>
<td>Points to an <strong>embedded</strong> resource</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Browser behavior</strong></td>
<td>Does not stop HTML parsing</td>
<td><code>&lt;script src&gt;</code> <strong>blocks</strong> HTML parsing un=
til downloaded &amp; executed (unless <code>async</code>/<code>defer</code>=
)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Relationship</strong></td>
<td>Navigational =E2=80=94 the resource supplements the document</td>
<td>Replacement =E2=80=94 the resource is placed <strong>into</strong> the =
document</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
