<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>localStorage</strong> is a web storage API in HTML5=
 that allows you to store key-value pairs in the browser with <strong>no ex=
piration</strong> =E2=80=94 data persists across browser sessions until exp=
licitly cleared.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Key characteristics:</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Storage capacity: ~5MB per domain</li>
<li>Data is never sent to the server</li>
<li>Accessible from any window/tab on the same origin</li>
<li>Stores data as strings</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Basic API:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative o=
verflow-auto" dir=3D"auto"><pre><span class=3D"pl-c">// Store data</span>
<span class=3D"pl-s1">localStorage</span><span class=3D"pl-kos">.</span><sp=
an class=3D"pl-en">setItem</span><span class=3D"pl-kos">(</span><span class=
=3D"pl-s">"name"</span><span class=3D"pl-kos">,</span> <span class=3D"pl-s"=
>"John"</span><span class=3D"pl-kos">)</span><span class=3D"pl-kos">;</span=
>

<span class=3D"pl-c">// Retrieve data</span>
<span class=3D"pl-s1">localStorage</span><span class=3D"pl-kos">.</span><sp=
an class=3D"pl-en">getItem</span><span class=3D"pl-kos">(</span><span class=
=3D"pl-s">"name"</span><span class=3D"pl-kos">)</span><span class=3D"pl-kos=
