<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Why rAF beats <code>setInterval</code>/<code>setTim=
eout</code> for animations:</strong></p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th></th>
<th><code>setInterval</code> / <code>setTimeout</code></th>
<th><code>requestAnimationFrame</code></th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Timing</td>
<td>Fixed timer =E2=80=94 may not align with screen refresh</td>
<td>Synchronized with display refresh (60fps)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Background tabs</td>
<td>Continues running, wastes CPU</td>
<td><strong>Paused automatically</strong> when tab is hidden</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Frame skips</td>
<td>Can fire multiple times per frame or miss frames</td>
<td>Fires exactly once per frame</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Battery drain</td>
<td>Higher</td>
<td>Lower =E2=80=94 browser can optimize</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Smooth animation</td>
<td>No =E2=80=94 may cause jank</td>
<td>Yes =E2=80=94 synchronized with rendering cycle</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
