<p dir=3D"auto">HTML5 drag-and-drop uses the <code>DOM event model</code> a=
nd <code>drag events</code> inherited from <code>mouse events</code>. A typ=
ical drag operation begins when a user selects a draggable element, drags t=
he element to a droppable element, and then releases the dragged element.</=
p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Event</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Drag</td>
<td>It fires every time when the mouse is moved while the object is being d=
ragged.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Dragstart</td>
<td>It is a very initial stage. It fires when the user starts dragging obje=
ct.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Dragenter</td>
<td>It fires when the user moves his/her mouse cursur over the target eleme=
nt.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Dragover</td>
<td>This event is fired when the mouse moves over an element.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Dragleave</td>
<td>This event is fired when the mouse leaves an element.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Drop</td>
<td>Drop It fires at the end of the drag operation.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Dragend</td>
<td>It fires when user releases the mouse button to complete the drag opera=
tion.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
