<p dir=3D"auto">The <code>DataTransfer</code> object carries data during a =
drag-and-drop operation. It is available on <code>DragEvent</code> objects =
and allows you to store, retrieve, and control what data is being transferr=
ed.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Key properties and methods:</strong></p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Member</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>dataTransfer.setData(format, data)</code></td>
<td>Store data with a MIME type key</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>dataTransfer.getData(format)</code></td>
<td>Retrieve stored data</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>dataTransfer.clearData([format])</code></td>
<td>Remove stored data</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>dataTransfer.effectAllowed</code></td>
<td>Defines allowed operations: <code>"copy"</code>, <code>"move"</code>, <=
code>"link"</code>, <code>"none"</code>, <code>"all"</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>dataTransfer.dropEffect</code></td>
<td>The actual effect during dragover: <code>"copy"</code>, <code>"move"</c=
ode>, <code>"link"</code>, <code>"none"</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>dataTransfer.files</code></td>
<td><code>FileList</code> of files being dragged (from OS)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>dataTransfer.items</code></td>
<td><code>DataTransferItemList</code> for multi-item data</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>dataTransfer.setDragImage(element, x, y)</code></td>
<td>Set a custom drag image</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
