<p dir=3D"auto">The <code>tabindex</code> attribute controls the order in w=
hich elements receive focus when the user navigates using the <strong>Tab</=
strong> key. It can be applied to any HTML element.</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Value</th>
<th>Behavior</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>tabindex=3D"0"</code></td>
<td>Element is focusable in natural DOM order</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>tabindex=3D"-1"</code></td>
<td>Focusable via JavaScript only (<code>element.focus()</code>), excluded =
from Tab sequence</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>tabindex=3D"n"</code> (positive)</td>
<td>Focused before elements with lower or no tabindex (avoid =E2=80=94 brea=
ks natural order)</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
