<p dir=3D"auto">Here are the key techniques to improve page load performanc=
e:</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Reduce HTTP Requests</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Combine JS files into one, CSS files into one</li>
<li>Use CSS sprites to merge multiple images into a single file</li>
<li>Remove duplicate scripts</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Assets &amp; Delivery</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Use a <strong>CDN</strong> =E2=80=94 serves content from servers geogra=
phically closer to users</li>
<li><strong>Gzip</strong> compression =E2=80=94 reduces HTTP response size =
by ~70%</li>
<li>Minify JavaScript and CSS</li>
<li>Make JS and CSS external so browsers can cache them</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Script &amp; Style Placement</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Put <code>&lt;link&gt;</code> stylesheets in <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> =
=E2=80=94 enables progressive rendering</li>
<li>Put <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> tags at the bottom of <code>&lt;body&gt=
;</code>, or use <code>async</code>/<code>defer</code></li>
</ul>
