<p dir=3D"auto">The <code>srcset</code> attribute allows to define a list o=
f different image resources along with size information so that browser can=
 pick the most appropriate image based on the actual device's resolution.</=
p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><code>srcset</code> lets you provide multiple image version=
s and let the browser pick the best one for the current device automaticall=
y.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">The Two Ways to Use <code>srcset</code></p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>1. Using display density descriptor(<code>x</code>)=
:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><code>srcset</code> provides a comma-separated list of imag=
e resources along with display density it should be used, for example1x, 2x=
 etc.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Example:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"highlight highlight-text-html-basic notranslate position-rela=
