<p dir=3D"auto">The <code>&lt;track&gt;</code> element is used inside <code=
>&lt;video&gt;</code> to provide timed text tracks such as subtitles, capti=
ons, chapters, and metadata.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Attributes of <code>&lt;track&gt;</code>:</strong><=
/p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Attribute</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>src</code></td>
<td>URL of the <code>.vtt</code> (WebVTT) or <code>.srt</code> subtitle fil=
e</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>kind</code></td>
<td><code>subtitles</code> / <code>captions</code> / <code>descriptions</co=
de> / <code>chapters</code> / <code>metadata</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>srclang</code></td>
<td>Language of the track (e.g., <code>en</code>, <code>fr</code>)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>label</code></td>
<td>Human-readable label shown in the browser UI</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>default</code></td>
<td>Enables this track by default</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Difference between subtitles and captions:</strong>=
</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li><strong>Subtitles</strong> =E2=80=94 translate dialogue for users who d=
on't speak the language</li>
<li><strong>Captions</strong> =E2=80=94 include dialogue + sound effects fo=
r deaf/hard-of-hearing users</li>
</ul>
