<p dir=3D"auto">The <strong>Intersection Observer API</strong> provides an =
asynchronous way to observe changes in the intersection (visibility) of a t=
arget element with its ancestor or the viewport. It is the recommended appr=
oach for implementing lazy loading, infinite scrolling, and animation trigg=
ers =E2=80=94 replacing expensive scroll event listeners.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Core concepts:</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li><strong>root</strong> =E2=80=94 the ancestor element used as the viewpo=
rt (defaults to browser viewport)</li>
<li><strong>rootMargin</strong> =E2=80=94 margin around the root (like CSS =
<code>margin</code>)</li>
<li><strong>threshold</strong> =E2=80=94 percentage of the target visible b=
efore the callback fires (0.0 to 1.0)</li>
</ul>
