<p dir=3D"auto">The <strong>History API</strong> (<code>window.history</cod=
e>) enables JavaScript to manipulate the browser's session history =E2=80=
=94 adding or modifying history entries =E2=80=94 without reloading the pag=
e. This is the foundation of <strong>Single Page Applications (SPAs)</stron=
g>.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Key methods:</strong></p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Method</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>history.pushState(state, title, url)</code></td>
<td>Add a new history entry</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>history.replaceState(state, title, url)</code></td>
<td>Replace the current history entry</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>history.back()</code></td>
<td>Go back one step (same as browser back button)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>history.forward()</code></td>
<td>Go forward one step</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>history.go(n)</code></td>
<td>Jump <code>n</code> steps (<code>-1</code> =3D back, <code>2</code> =3D=
 forward two)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>history.length</code></td>
<td>Number of entries in the session history</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
