<p dir=3D"auto">The <strong>File API</strong> provides a way to read and in=
teract with files that users select via <code>&lt;input type=3D"file"&gt;</=
code> or drag-and-drop, entirely on the client side =E2=80=94 without uploa=
ding to a server.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Key interfaces:</strong></p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Interface</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>File</code></td>
<td>Represents a single file; extends <code>Blob</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>FileList</code></td>
<td>Array-like list of <code>File</code> objects from an <code>&lt;input&gt=
;</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>FileReader</code></td>
<td>Reads the content of a <code>File</code> or <code>Blob</code> asynchron=
ously</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Blob</code></td>
<td>Raw binary data; <code>File</code> is a specialized <code>Blob</code></=
td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
