<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>MathML (Mathematical Markup Language)</strong> is a=
n XML-based markup language for describing mathematical notation. It is nat=
ively supported inside HTML5 using the <code>&lt;math&gt;</code> element, a=
llowing mathematical expressions to be rendered by the browser without imag=
es or JavaScript libraries.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Two types of MathML:</strong></p>
<ol dir=3D"auto">
<li><strong>Presentation MathML</strong> =E2=80=94 controls how math <em>lo=
oks</em> (most commonly used)</li>
<li><strong>Content MathML</strong> =E2=80=94 describes the mathematical <e=
m>meaning</em></li>
</ol>
