<p dir=3D"auto"><strong><code>hreflang</code></strong> is an HTML attribute=
 used to tell search engines which language and/or geographic region a page=
 is intended for. It helps Google serve the correct regional or language va=
riant to users.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>When to use:</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Your site has content in multiple languages (e.g., English, French, Spa=
nish)</li>
<li>Your site has region-specific versions (e.g., <code>en-US</code>, <code=
>en-GB</code>, <code>en-AU</code>)</li>
<li>Your site has translated pages with different URLs</li>
</ul>
