<p dir=3D"auto">HTML entities are special character codes used to represent=
 characters that have a reserved meaning in HTML (like <code>&lt;</code>, <=
code>&gt;</code>, <code>&amp;</code>) or that are not easily typeable.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Syntax:</strong> <code>&amp;name;</code> or <code>&=
amp;#number;</code> (decimal) or <code>&amp;#xHEX;</code> (hex)</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Common entities:</strong></p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Character</th>
<th>Entity Name</th>
<th>Entity Number</th>
<th>Use case</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>&lt;</code></td>
<td><code>&amp;lt;</code></td>
<td><code>&amp;#60;</code></td>
<td>Less-than (HTML tag delimiter)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>&gt;</code></td>
<td><code>&amp;gt;</code></td>
<td><code>&amp;#62;</code></td>
<td>Greater-than (HTML tag delimiter)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>&amp;</code></td>
<td><code>&amp;amp;</code></td>
<td><code>&amp;#38;</code></td>
<td>Ampersand (entity start character)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>"</code></td>
<td><code>&amp;quot;</code></td>
<td><code>&amp;#34;</code></td>
<td>Quote inside attribute values</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>'</code></td>
<td><code>&amp;apos;</code></td>
<td><code>&amp;#39;</code></td>
<td>Apostrophe inside attribute values</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code> </code> (non-breaking space)</td>
<td><code>&amp;nbsp;</code></td>
<td><code>&amp;#160;</code></td>
<td>Prevent line break between words</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>=C2=A9</code></td>
<td><code>&amp;copy;</code></td>
<td><code>&amp;#169;</code></td>
<td>Copyright symbol</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>=C2=AE</code></td>
<td><code>&amp;reg;</code></td>
<td><code>&amp;#174;</code></td>
<td>Registered trademark</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>=E2=86=92</code></td>
<td><code>&amp;rarr;</code></td>
<td><code>&amp;#8594;</code></td>
<td>Right arrow</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
