<p dir=3D"auto">HTML5 provides built-in client-side form validation without=
 JavaScript, using <strong>constraint validation attributes</strong> on for=
m controls. The browser validates automatically on submit and shows native =
error messages.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Key attributes:</strong></p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Attribute</th>
<th>Applies to</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>required</code></td>
<td>All inputs</td>
<td>Field must not be empty</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>minlength</code> / <code>maxlength</code></td>
<td><code>text</code>, <code>email</code>, <code>password</code>, <code>tex=
tarea</code></td>
<td>Min/max character count</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>min</code> / <code>max</code></td>
<td><code>number</code>, <code>date</code>, <code>range</code></td>
<td>Min/max value</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>pattern</code></td>
<td><code>text</code>, <code>email</code>, <code>tel</code>, <code>url</cod=
e></td>
<td>RegExp the value must match</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>type</code></td>
<td><code>&lt;input&gt;</code></td>
<td><code>email</code>, <code>url</code>, <code>number</code> validate form=
at automatically</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>step</code></td>
<td><code>number</code>, <code>date</code>, <code>range</code></td>
<td>Valid value intervals</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
