<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Shadow DOM</strong> is a browser API that allows yo=
u to attach an <strong>encapsulated, isolated DOM subtree</strong> to an el=
ement =E2=80=94 separate from the main document DOM. Styles and scripts ins=
ide the shadow DOM do not leak out, and external styles cannot accidentally=
 affect it.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Key concepts:</strong></p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Term</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Shadow host</td>
<td>The regular DOM element that the shadow DOM is attached to</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Shadow root</td>
<td>The root node of the shadow tree (<code>attachShadow()</code> returns t=
his)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Shadow tree</td>
<td>The DOM subtree inside the shadow root</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Light DOM</td>
<td>The regular document DOM (as opposed to the shadow DOM)</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
