<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Custom Elements</strong> allow developers to define=
 new HTML tags with their own behavior and lifecycle callbacks. They are on=
e of the four Web Components standards (Custom Elements, Shadow DOM, HTML T=
emplates, ES Modules).</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Two types:</strong></p>
<ol dir=3D"auto">
<li><strong>Autonomous custom elements</strong> =E2=80=94 extend <code>HTML=
Element</code> directly, create a brand-new tag</li>
<li><strong>Customized built-in elements</strong> =E2=80=94 extend an exist=
ing HTML element (e.g., <code>HTMLButtonElement</code>)</li>
</ol>
