<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Subresource Integrity (SRI)</strong> is a security =
feature that allows browsers to verify that files loaded from third-party s=
ources (CDNs) have not been tampered with. The browser computes a cryptogra=
phic hash of the downloaded file and compares it to the expected hash in th=
e <code>integrity</code> attribute. If they don't match, the resource is bl=
ocked.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Syntax:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"highlight highlight-text-html-basic notranslate position-rela=
