1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.00=
2 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-=
.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.=
042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5=
a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.9=
98 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a>=
</div>
<p dir=3D"auto">The <code>sandbox</code> attribute on <code>&lt;iframe&gt;<=
/code> applies a set of <strong>extra restrictions</strong> to the content =
of the iframe. By default, <code>sandbox</code> with no value restricts alm=
ost everything. You can selectively allow capabilities by adding specific t=
oken values.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Default behavior with <code>sandbox</code> (no valu=
es) =E2=80=94 ALL of these are blocked:</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Script execution</li>
<li>Form submission</li>
<li>Popups and new windows</li>
<li>Access to parent frame (<code>window.parent</code>)</li>
<li>Same-origin access (treated as a different origin)</li>
<li>Plugin loading</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Selective allow tokens:</strong></p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Token</th>
<th>Allows</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>allow-scripts</code></td>
<td>JavaScript execution</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>allow-forms</code></td>
<td>Form submission</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>allow-same-origin</code></td>
<td>Same-origin access (use with caution)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>allow-popups</code></td>
<td><code>window.open()</code>, <code>target=3D"_blank"</code> links</td>
</tr>
